{
  "dom_id": "step-615693",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Applying a Percentage Increase",
  "problem": "What number is $40\\%$ greater than $360?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find a number $40\\%$ *greater than* $360,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\% + 40\\% = 140\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140\\% = \\dfrac{140}{100} = 1.40\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $40\\%$ greater than $360,$ we multiply $360$ by $1.40{:}$\n\n$$\n1.40 \\cdot 360 = 504\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $40\\%$ greater than $360$ is $504.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
